{
  "title": "Systolic reading curvature adds no demonstrated CRP prediction gain across two NHANES cycles",
  "abstract": "In 3,100 NHANES 2005\u20132006 adults and 4,538 separately sampled 2007\u20132008 adults, signed systolic BP curvature did not improve concurrent log CRP prediction beyond demographics, adiposity, mean BP and systolic SD: target weighted MSE increased by 0.001209 (0.1033%); full source-plus-target bootstrap 95% interval [-0.001114, 0.006867]. This is a scoped negative prediction result, not evidence of no physiological information.",
